1
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:13,800
(Let it go.)

2
00:00:43,724 --> 00:00:45,964
=Revenge From A Wife=

3
00:00:46,091 --> 00:00:48,317
=Episode 29=

4
00:01:07,119 --> 00:01:08,560
Roujia.

5
00:01:10,439 --> 00:01:12,640
I've come to see you.

6
00:01:23,599 --> 00:01:24,920
These past few years,

7
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:28,120
I've done a great deal.

8
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:30,560
(Late Empress Roujia's Memorial Tablet)
Those who harmed you

9
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:33,239
have all paid the price.

10
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:36,519
I saw justice done

11
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:40,120
for over 100 wronged craftsmen.

12
00:01:41,079 --> 00:01:42,480
And your good name,

13
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:44,640
I protected that too.

14
00:01:45,079 --> 00:01:47,680
I let none of that filth

15
00:01:48,599 --> 00:01:51,760
tarnish it in the slightest.

16
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:55,079
At court and across the realm,

17
00:01:55,239 --> 00:01:57,799
they call me a benevolent ruler.

18
00:01:58,959 --> 00:02:01,079
A white deer has appeared,

19
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:04,000
a once-in-a-millennium auspicious omen.

20
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:05,680
Roujia.

21
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,680
If your spirit is watching,

22
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,359
you know I haven't failed you.

23
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,680
And from where you are,

24
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:21,560
you must protect me.

25
00:02:22,039 --> 00:02:23,759
Let me

26
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,120
recover soon.

27
00:02:26,759 --> 00:02:29,439
I still have much to do

28
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:32,360
and greater deeds to accomplish.

29
00:02:33,599 --> 00:02:36,000
I'm a benevolent ruler.

30
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,919
Heaven

31
00:02:38,759 --> 00:02:41,120
wouldn't want me dead.

32
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:43,560
You wouldn't either,

33
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:45,400
would you?

34
00:02:50,719 --> 00:02:52,240
Su.

35
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,800
Don't you agree?

36
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,879
After all Your Majesty has done,

37
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:02,560
Heaven will surely favor you.

38
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,599
I'm sleepy.

39
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,080
So sleepy.

40
00:03:21,879 --> 00:03:23,680
You've had a long day, Your Majesty.

41
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,280
You should rest.

42
00:03:36,960 --> 00:03:37,840
Your Majesty.

43
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,080
Get some sleep.

44
00:04:06,759 --> 00:04:08,680
That scent...

45
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:12,360
I haven't smelled it in a long time.

46
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,080
Your Majesty, you have quite a memory.

47
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,520
I burned this wild grass

48
00:04:19,159 --> 00:04:20,680
when we first met.

49
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:23,759
Common folk can't afford ambergris

50
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,439
or sandalwood,

51
00:04:25,759 --> 00:04:28,079
so they dry wild grass and burn it.

52
00:04:28,279 --> 00:04:29,360
It keeps mosquitoes away

53
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,439
and helps calm the mind.

54
00:04:30,839 --> 00:04:32,480
Back when I lived outside the palace,

55
00:04:32,879 --> 00:04:34,240
I smelled it every day.

56
00:04:47,439 --> 00:04:49,240
That screen...

57
00:04:49,959 --> 00:04:52,079
Has it been replaced?

58
00:04:56,639 --> 00:04:58,000
You noticed, Your Majesty.

59
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,920
On the old screen,

60
00:05:01,360 --> 00:05:04,439
"Peace and Prosperity for All" showed

61
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,800
a faint red mark in the dragon's eye,

62
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,639
as if one stroke brought it to life.

63
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,720
But this one

64
00:05:16,759 --> 00:05:18,920
is spotless.

65
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:25,480
On the old screen,

66
00:05:26,279 --> 00:05:28,120
that red stroke in the dragon's eye

67
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,160
wasn't cinnabar.

68
00:05:30,879 --> 00:05:32,920
It was blood from a slain craftsman,

69
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,759
splashed there as he died.

70
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:38,519
He was a master craftsman.

71
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,839
Even his simple grass weaving

72
00:05:40,959 --> 00:05:42,959
was finer than embroidery.

73
00:05:44,519 --> 00:05:46,240
The day the screen was put up,

74
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:50,560
he was brutally beaten to death before
"Peace and Prosperity for All."

75
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,720
When the final blow fell,

76
00:05:53,839 --> 00:05:55,200
his blood sprayed up

77
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,240
and splashed onto the dragon's eye.

78
00:05:58,199 --> 00:05:59,680
That gave the screen its soul.

79
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,920
It was Consort Chen's gift,

80
00:06:03,399 --> 00:06:05,160
and that craftsman's tombstone.

81
00:06:13,079 --> 00:06:14,839
That's why I felt it was wrong

82
00:06:15,199 --> 00:06:17,840
to leave a dead man's blood
in the cottage.

83
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,959
It might disturb the late Empress.

84
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,120
That wouldn't be right.

85
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,840
So I took it upon myself

86
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,480
to replace it with a new screen.

87
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,240
What is the meaning of this?

88
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:38,680
Don't you always say

89
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:40,640
you want to know the people's hearts?

90
00:06:43,399 --> 00:06:44,840
This new screen

91
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,480
has a name too.

92
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,320
It's called
"Winning the People's Hearts."

93
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,200
I took the liberty

94
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:10,520
of showing you where their hearts lie.

95
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,840
Would Your Majesty like to see

96
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:14,720
what truly lies

97
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,320
in their hearts?

98
00:07:19,319 --> 00:07:20,639
Su.

99
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:23,920
What exactly are you trying to do?

100
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,079
(Wretched Emperor!)

101
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:52,560
(Bones pile up at the cottage.)

102
00:07:52,560 --> 00:07:54,040
(The Emperor revels in song and dance.)

103
00:07:54,199 --> 00:07:56,360
(A murderous hypocrite!)

104
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:58,360
(One tael of silver)

105
00:07:58,439 --> 00:08:00,839
(for my father's life.)

106
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,439
(Empress Roujia,)

107
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:05,720
(open your eyes and look at this beast.)

108
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:08,399
(A coward in imperial robes!)

109
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,120
Do you see now?

110
00:08:15,439 --> 00:08:16,079
This...

111
00:08:16,560 --> 00:08:18,279
is what's truly in the people's hearts.

112
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,240
How dare you!

113
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:48,307
♪Sunset fades beyond the lonely city♪

114
00:08:48,441 --> 00:08:52,054
♪Dusk snow paints the green hills♪

115
00:08:52,289 --> 00:08:54,888
♪A lone rider storms the old pass♪

116
00:08:54,925 --> 00:08:57,205
♪Drunk, I gaze by lamplight♪

117
00:08:57,252 --> 00:09:01,081
♪Old friends have all drifted away♪

118
00:09:01,483 --> 00:09:04,836
♪My broken sword rusts, as do I♪

119
00:09:05,763 --> 00:09:09,276
♪Jackdaws cry into the night♪

120
00:09:09,776 --> 00:09:12,343
♪Half a banner snaps in the wind♪

121
00:09:12,469 --> 00:09:14,502
♪In dreams, I return to the camps♪

122
00:09:14,569 --> 00:09:18,346
♪Moonlight chills my armor♪

123
00:09:18,696 --> 00:09:23,029
♪Life is a dream through many winters♪

124
00:09:23,252 --> 00:09:26,759
♪I gaze beyond the edge of the world♪

125
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:29,793
♪Parting sorrow spills across the moon♪

126
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:35,474
♪The moon and wind mean nothing now♪

127
00:09:35,514 --> 00:09:38,528
♪History turns to ash before ink dries♪

128
00:09:38,569 --> 00:09:44,577
♪Who plays the zither
and sighs at the pavilion?♪

129
00:09:45,244 --> 00:09:52,199
♪The past has faded away♪

130
00:09:52,199 --> 00:09:56,231
♪The past has faded away♪
